Well, Jenna, I went and found my MySpace blogs, so they're not online anymore.
好吧，珍娜，我去找了我的MySpace博客，它们现在已经不在网上了。

632
00:24:30.870 --> 00:24:35.750
I don't know why, but I guess I had printed them out at some point.
我不知道为什么，但我想我当年在某个时候把它们打印出来了。

633
00:24:36.190 --> 00:24:43.390
So now I'm going to start going to them for each episode, and I did for this one, but I'll save it for a bit, because it happens later in the episode.
所以现在我打算为每一集都去翻翻它们，这一集我也看了，但我先留着不剧透，因为那是这集后面才发生的事。

634
00:24:43.490 --> 00:24:44.050
Okay, great.
好的，太棒了。

635
00:24:44.230 --> 00:24:47.110
Fan question from small actor in a peacoat.
来自“穿着呢子大衣的矮个演员”的粉丝提问。

636
00:24:47.110 --> 00:24:51.070
Who kept the camera with all of the pictures that Michael took?
谁保留了迈克拍的所有照片的相机？

637
00:24:51.870 --> 00:24:52.270
NBC.
NBC。

638
00:24:52.910 --> 00:24:56.750
Yeah, they were property of NBC, and they had them up on their website for a while.
对，它们是NBC的财产，而且它们在他们的网站上挂了一段时间。

639
00:24:56.950 --> 00:24:57.830
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

640
00:24:57.950 --> 00:24:59.150
You can still find them.
你现在还能找到它们。

641
00:24:59.250 --> 00:24:59.370
Yes.
是的。

642
00:24:59.370 --> 00:25:00.730
And Jenna and I were texting last night.
我和珍娜昨晚还发短信来着。

643
00:25:00.850 --> 00:25:03.610
We both found them over at officetally.com.
我们俩都在officetally.com上找到了。

644
00:25:03.790 --> 00:25:07.430
Yeah, so you can see all those pictures that he was really taking pictures.
对，所以你能看到他当时真的在拍的那些照片。

645
00:25:07.670 --> 00:25:11.830
Yeah, and they're really, like, not centered, and, like, people's heads are cut off.
对，而且它们真的就……没有对准中心，而且人们的头都被截掉了。

646
00:25:11.930 --> 00:25:15.390
It's as if he just went around clicking away, but there's some real gems in there.
就好像他只是到处乱按快门一样，但里面确实有一些真正的宝藏。

647
00:25:15.510 --> 00:25:15.930
I know.
我知道。

648
00:25:15.930 --> 00:25:18.390
Six minutes, 54 seconds.
六分五十四秒。

649
00:25:19.030 --> 00:25:27.590
Michael really, really shows what he thinks about Christmas, which is a gift should say, I love you, this many dollars worth.
迈克真的、真的很清楚地表达了他对圣诞节的看法，那就是：一份礼物应该表达“我爱你有这么多钱的价值”。

650
00:25:27.830 --> 00:25:28.050
Yeah.
对。

651
00:25:28.390 --> 00:25:30.370
Oh, this is not going to go well.
哦，这下要糟了。

652
00:25:30.610 --> 00:25:41.810
Well, speaking of gifts, we have a scene where Toby reveals what he got Angela in Secret Santa, and it is the Jazz Baby poster.
说到礼物，我们有个情节是托比透露了他给安吉拉抽到的秘密圣诞老人礼物，也就是那张爵士宝贝海报。

653
00:25:42.070 --> 00:25:42.250
Yeah.
对。

654
00:25:42.670 --> 00:25:44.630
I have that poster, guys.
我有那张海报，伙计们。

655
00:25:44.710 --> 00:25:45.430
You have it?
你有？

656
00:25:45.430 --> 00:25:48.110
That was one of my questions from Chris Cordova.
那是克里斯·科尔多瓦提出的问题之一。

657
00:25:48.330 --> 00:25:50.610
He wants to know, did you keep the baby poster?
他想知道，你留着那张婴儿海报吗？

658
00:25:50.770 --> 00:25:52.190
Well, there was about 20 of them.
嗯，大概有二十张呢。

659
00:25:52.330 --> 00:25:52.410
Yeah.
对。

660
00:25:52.410 --> 00:25:53.250
They had made a bunch.
他们制作了一大批。

661
00:25:53.630 --> 00:25:55.950
One hung by my desk for years.
其中一张挂在我办公桌旁好几年。

662
00:25:56.150 --> 00:25:56.470
Yes.
没错。

663
00:25:56.730 --> 00:25:56.990
Yeah.
对。

664
00:25:56.990 --> 00:26:01.050
So, we got to see it every day, and I have one.
所以，我们每天都能看到它，而且我有一张。

665
00:26:01.290 --> 00:26:03.570
It's rolled up in a little poster thingy.
它被卷在一个小海报筒里。

666
00:26:03.570 --> 00:26:05.890
Now, do you know the story behind that picture?
那么，你知道那张照片背后的故事吗？

667
00:26:05.890 --> 00:26:08.730
Because I traded some text messages with Phil Shea.
因为我和菲尔·谢伊发过一些短信。

668
00:26:08.970 --> 00:26:09.390
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

669
00:26:09.610 --> 00:26:13.430
So, Phil Shea had to make that poster.
所以，菲尔·谢伊必须制作那张海报。

670
00:26:13.590 --> 00:26:14.730
He did not buy that poster.
他可不是买的。

671
00:26:14.850 --> 00:26:16.970
He put out a casting call for babies.
他发布了婴儿的选角通知。

672
00:26:16.970 --> 00:26:18.670
And two babies were caSt.
结果选定了两个婴儿。

673
00:26:18.830 --> 00:26:18.990
Yes.
对。

674
00:26:18.990 --> 00:26:19.650
Baby actors.
婴儿演员。

675
00:26:20.010 --> 00:26:24.070
He said it was really hard to find tiny jazz instruments.
他说要找到微型的爵士乐器真的很难。

676
00:26:25.730 --> 00:26:27.370
He said that was really difficult.
他说那真的非常困难。

677
00:26:27.690 --> 00:26:30.710
In fact, he said, you know, Amazon didn't exist back then.
事实上，他说，你知道的，那时候还没有亚马逊。

678
00:26:31.370 --> 00:26:34.270
You know, you couldn't just Google baby jazz instrument.
你知道的，你不能随便在谷歌上搜婴儿爵士乐器。

679
00:26:35.370 --> 00:26:38.110
And they couldn't be fake-looking.
而且它们不能看起来是假的。

680
00:26:38.250 --> 00:26:39.910
Like, they couldn't be, like, blue and pink.
比如，它们不能是蓝色的和粉红色的。

681
00:26:40.270 --> 00:26:44.050
So, he did eventually find them at a place called Hollywood Costumes.
所以，他最终确实在一家叫好莱坞服装店的地方找到了。

682
00:26:44.310 --> 00:26:47.510
He was particularly proud of the tiny sunglasses that he found.
他对自己找到的那些微型太阳镜感到格外自豪。

683
00:26:47.510 --> 00:26:50.170
This poster ends up coming back in conflict resolution.
这张海报最后在冲突解决那一集里再次出现。

684
00:26:50.170 --> 00:26:53.410
Like you said, it stayed up there, but then it comes back again.
就像你说的，它一直挂在那儿，但接着又出现了。

685
00:26:53.530 --> 00:26:54.350
It comes back again.
它又出现了。

686
00:26:54.350 --> 00:26:57.710
I would like to know the two babies that were in the poster.
我很想知道海报里的那两个婴儿是谁。

687
00:26:57.870 --> 00:26:58.830
Oh, guys.
哦，天哪。

688
00:26:59.130 --> 00:27:00.090
Where are they today?
他们现在在哪里？

689
00:27:00.710 --> 00:27:07.750
If you are a baby from the baby jazz poster, will you please write to us at officeladies
如果你就是爵士婴儿海报里的那个婴儿，请给我们写信，邮箱是 officeladies

690
00:27:07.750 --> 00:27:09.370
at earwolf.com?
at earwolf.com？

691
00:27:09.470 --> 00:27:12.930
One thing about that baby jazz poster, I remember Mike Schur telling me that they thought it was
关于那张爵士婴儿海报，我记得迈克·舒尔跟我说过，他们觉得安吉拉会真的很喜欢打扮成成年人的婴儿，这非常搞笑。

692
00:27:12.930 --> 00:27:18.410
really funny that Angela would really enjoy babies dressed as adults.
好吧。

693
00:27:18.710 --> 00:27:19.250
Okay.
我们讲到哪儿了？

694
00:27:19.470 --> 00:27:20.330
Where are we?
嗯，我们在谈论礼物。

695
00:27:20.530 --> 00:27:22.470
Well, we're talking about the gifts.
迈克·舒尔其实说过，这些礼物极其难以管理。

696
00:27:22.870 --> 00:27:27.470
And Mike Schur actually said that the gifts were incredibly hard to manage.
因为它们是从秘密圣诞老人开始的。

697
00:27:27.930 --> 00:27:30.110
Because they start off as Secret Santa.
所以，每个人都有一个他们专门为其购买礼物的人。

698
00:27:30.110 --> 00:27:33.210
So, everybody had a person that they bought a specific gift for.
然后你必须追踪这些礼物在 Yankee swap（白象交换礼物）中是如何流转的。

699
00:27:33.410 --> 00:27:37.550
And then you had to track the gifts as they went around in the Yankee swap.
事实上，在本集的剧本中，有一整页都在列出这些礼物。

700
00:27:37.810 --> 00:27:45.030
He actually, in the script of this episode, there is a whole page where he lists the gifts.
（译注：此处原文无误，语境连贯）

701
00:27:45.350 --> 00:27:46.810
Who bought who what?
谁给谁买了什么？

702
00:27:46.810 --> 00:27:50.490
And he did this for Veda, our script supervisor.
而且他这是为薇达做的，我们的剧本统筹。

703
00:27:50.830 --> 00:27:57.070
We haven't really talked about her, but Veda's job is to sit and watch every take that is filmed
我们还没怎么聊过她，不过薇达的工作就是坐在那儿看拍下的每一个镜头，

704
00:27:57.070 --> 00:28:01.090
and make notes about everything that happens continuity-wise.
并记下所有与连戏有关的事情。

705
00:28:01.490 --> 00:28:03.430
So, I mean, like, really specific.
所以，我的意思是，真的非常具体。

706
00:28:03.730 --> 00:28:09.790
So, like, if in a scene you take a drink of your tea on a certain line and then scratch your nose on
所以，如果在某个镜头里你在某句台词时喝了口茶，然后在另一句时

707
00:28:09.790 --> 00:28:14.910
another one, Veda writes it down so that you do it the same every time for editing purposes.
挠了挠鼻子，薇达就会记下来，为了剪辑的目的，让你每次都做得一模一样。

708
00:28:15.250 --> 00:28:15.390
Yeah.
对。

709
00:28:15.650 --> 00:28:21.810
Veda would come up to us and say, Angela, you were holding that pen in your left hand in the first take.
薇达会走到我们跟前说，安吉拉，第一个镜头里你左手拿着那支笔。

710
00:28:22.030 --> 00:28:24.770
And in the second take, you picked it up and held it in your right hand.
到了第二个镜头，你把它拿起来换到右手拿了。

711
00:28:25.210 --> 00:28:26.450
So, that's not going to match.
所以，这样就接不上了。

712
00:28:26.590 --> 00:28:30.290
So, you need to pick which hand you're going to hold that pen in and do it in every take the same way.
因此，你得选好到底要用哪只手拿那支笔，然后每个镜头都用同样的方式拿。

713
00:28:30.290 --> 00:28:35.150
Yeah, because otherwise, when you edit it together, the pen is magically bouncing from hand to hand.
对，因为否则的话，当你把它们剪辑到一起时，那支笔就会像变魔术一样在两只手里跳来跳去。

714
00:28:35.910 --> 00:28:40.910
So, Mike was really worried about Veda in this episode.
所以，迈克这一集里真的挺担心薇达的。

715
00:28:41.310 --> 00:28:44.390
And so, he made this list just for Veda.
于是，他专门为薇达列了这张清单。

716
00:28:44.530 --> 00:28:46.130
And I have it from the script.
而且我是从剧本里拿到的。

717
00:28:46.350 --> 00:28:47.350
Oh, fantastic.
哦，太棒了。

718
00:28:47.490 --> 00:28:51.650
Okay, so this is what everyone was intended to give.
好的，所以这就是本来打算送给每个人的礼物。

719
00:28:51.750 --> 00:28:53.530
And we got a lot of fan questions about this.
我们收到了很多关于这个的粉丝提问。

720
00:28:53.630 --> 00:28:59.530
Like, a lot of people wrote in and said, you know, eventually Michael's going to get the paintball lessons from Dwight.
比如，很多人写信来说，你知道的，迈克尔最终会从德怀特那里得到彩弹射击课。

721
00:28:59.530 --> 00:29:02.410
But they're like, who did Dwight intend that to go to?
但他们想知道，德怀特原本打算把这个送给谁？

722
00:29:02.630 --> 00:29:04.330
So, I have all the answers right here.
所以，我这里有所有的答案。

723
00:29:04.430 --> 00:29:04.770
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

724
00:29:04.970 --> 00:29:05.230
Yeah.
准备好了。

725
00:29:05.790 --> 00:29:05.990
Okay.
好的。

726
00:29:06.670 --> 00:29:10.630
Dwight got Phyllis the paintball lessons and the pellets.
德怀特给菲莉丝买的是彩弹射击课和彩弹丸。

727
00:29:10.650 --> 00:29:12.290
That was his gift to Phyllis.
那是他送给菲莉丝的礼物。

728
00:29:12.930 --> 00:29:14.930
Phyllis made Michael an oven mitt.
菲莉丝给迈克尔做了一个隔热手套。

729
00:29:15.830 --> 00:29:17.750
Michael got Ryan an iPod.
迈克尔给瑞安买了一个iPod。

730
00:29:18.050 --> 00:29:23.670
Ryan got Toby a book of short stories by George Saunders, who happens to be one of Mike Schur's favorite writers.
瑞安给托比买了一本乔治·桑德斯的短篇小说集，他正好是迈克·舒尔最喜欢的作家之一。

731
00:29:24.110 --> 00:29:26.110
Toby got Angela the baby poster.
托比给安吉拉买了那张婴儿海报。

732
00:29:26.550 --> 00:29:28.730
Angela bought Stanley a picture frame.
安吉拉给斯坦利买了一个相框。

733
00:29:29.530 --> 00:29:31.530
Stanley got Kelly a nameplate.
斯坦利给凯利买了一个名牌。

734
00:29:31.970 --> 00:29:34.150
Kelly got Oscar a shower radio.
凯利给奥斯卡买了一个淋浴收音机。

735
00:29:34.770 --> 00:29:37.110
Oscar got Creed a shamrock keychain.
奥斯卡给克里德买了一个三叶草钥匙扣。

736
00:29:37.470 --> 00:29:40.190
Creed got Jim one of his own shirts.
克里德给吉姆买了他自己的衬衫之一。

737
00:29:40.930 --> 00:29:42.610
Jim got Pam the teapot.
吉姆给帕姆买了一个茶壶。

738
00:29:42.750 --> 00:29:44.550
And this is something that got cut out.
而这是被剪掉的内容。

739
00:29:44.850 --> 00:29:47.590
Pam made Meredith a drawing of The Office.
帕姆给梅雷迪思画了一幅办公室的画。

740
00:29:47.970 --> 00:29:49.710
I read about that online.
我在网上看到过这个。

741
00:29:49.990 --> 00:29:51.590
Yeah, and there was this big thing.
对，而且当时有这么个大事件。

742
00:29:51.810 --> 00:29:53.170
It's in the deleted scenes.
它在删除片段里。

743
00:29:53.370 --> 00:29:54.910
This is something I have to tell you.
这是我必须告诉你的一件事。

744
00:29:54.910 --> 00:29:57.010
I got a DVD player for Christmas.
我圣诞节收到了一台DVD播放器。

745
00:29:57.370 --> 00:29:57.710
What?
什么？

746
00:29:58.030 --> 00:30:00.110
My husband got me a DVD player.
我丈夫给我买了一台DVD播放器。

747
00:30:00.270 --> 00:30:01.950
So I got the CDs.
所以我拿到了光盘。

748
00:30:01.950 --> 00:30:03.530
He bought me the CD set.
他给我买了一套光盘。

749
00:30:03.690 --> 00:30:05.250
And I got a DVD player.
然后我得到了一台DVD播放器。

750
00:30:05.410 --> 00:30:08.190
And last night, I got to watch all the deleted scenes.
昨晚，我得以观看了所有的删除片段。

751
00:30:08.190 --> 00:30:10.650
Oh, Angela, you must be so happy.
哦，安吉拉，你一定高兴坏了。

752
00:30:10.670 --> 00:30:11.550
I was so happy.
我曾经很高兴。

753
00:30:11.550 --> 00:30:12.530
And there's so many.
而且有那么多。

754
00:30:12.870 --> 00:30:13.310
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

755
00:30:13.550 --> 00:30:13.990
There's so many.
有那么多。

756
00:30:14.110 --> 00:30:18.010
For the Christmas episode, you guys, there are so many great deleted scenes.
关于圣诞节那一集，大家，有那么多精彩的删减片段。

757
00:30:18.170 --> 00:30:19.990
I don't want to get us off topic here.
我不想让我们偏离正题。

758
00:30:20.410 --> 00:30:24.990
But there in the deleted scenes, Meredith opens up her painting.
但是在删减片段里，梅雷迪思打开了她的画作。

759
00:30:24.990 --> 00:30:26.470
That is from Pam.
那是来自帕姆的。

760
00:30:26.610 --> 00:30:27.790
And it's a drawing of The Office.
那是办公室的素描。

761
00:30:29.050 --> 00:30:30.710
Well, there's a big backstory here.
嗯，这里有一个很大的幕后故事。

762
00:30:30.890 --> 00:30:34.810
Again, with Phil, I don't do Pam's drawings.
再说一次，关于菲尔，我不画帕姆的画。

763
00:30:35.010 --> 00:30:36.210
People ask me that all the time.
人们总是问我这个问题。

764
00:30:36.390 --> 00:30:37.790
I'm not an artiSt.
我不是艺术家。

765
00:30:38.190 --> 00:30:42.390
I mean, we've talked about this, or have we, that I do cartoons.
我的意思是，我们讨论过这个，或者说没有，我画的是漫画。

766
00:30:42.410 --> 00:30:43.530
I do cartooning.
我画漫画。

767
00:30:43.650 --> 00:30:45.010
She's very good at cartooning.
她很擅长画漫画。

768
00:30:45.110 --> 00:30:46.950
And I have a few that you've drawn that I've saved.
我确实保存了几幅你画的。

769
00:30:47.110 --> 00:30:48.270
I think you're fantastic.
我觉得你太棒了。

770
00:30:48.750 --> 00:30:50.790
Well, I love my little expressive cartoons.
嗯，我喜欢我那些富于表现力的小漫画。

771
00:30:51.010 --> 00:30:54.570
But I needed Pam and wanted Pam to be a better artist than I am.
但我需要而且希望帕姆比我更有艺术天赋。

772
00:30:54.990 --> 00:30:58.990
So there is a young art student that does all of Pam's drawings.
所以有一个年轻的美术系学生画了帕姆所有的画。

773
00:30:59.210 --> 00:31:07.890
They went out to a bunch of people, like 12 different artists, to turn in samples to
他们找了很多人，大约12位不同的艺术家，来提交样本

774
00:31:07.890 --> 00:31:10.070
be the artist behind Pam.
来成为帕姆背后的画家。

775
00:31:10.250 --> 00:31:11.550
And they picked a young woman.
然后他们选了一位年轻女性。

776
00:31:12.030 --> 00:31:14.390
Now, Jenna, I read, and you can tell me if this is true.
詹娜，我读到过，你可以告诉我这是否属实。

777
00:31:14.570 --> 00:31:20.790
I read that the first painting that they had for this episode to give to Meredith from
我读到说这一集里给梅雷迪思的、本该来自帕姆的第一幅画，

778
00:31:20.790 --> 00:31:26.650
Pam, that they had one of our set art people, who was a man, do it.
是让我们的一位布景美术人员（是个男的）画的。

779
00:31:26.770 --> 00:31:26.950
Yeah.
是的。

780
00:31:27.130 --> 00:31:29.030
And when they looked at it, it looked too masculine.
当他们看的时候，觉得太有阳刚之气了。

781
00:31:29.250 --> 00:31:29.490
Yeah.
是的。

782
00:31:29.690 --> 00:31:31.830
And so then they went out to female artists.
所以他们才去找女艺术家。

783
00:31:31.990 --> 00:31:32.450
That's true.
是真的。

784
00:31:32.610 --> 00:31:33.830
To have a little bit of a softer touch.
为了带有一点更柔和的风格。

785
00:31:34.030 --> 00:31:34.210
Yeah.
是的。

786
00:31:34.390 --> 00:31:37.630
And there were something like 12 different artists who all submitted their work.
大约有12位不同的艺术家都提交了他们的作品。

787
00:31:38.450 --> 00:31:39.730
And I wish I knew her name.
我希望我知道她的名字。

788
00:31:39.850 --> 00:31:40.790
Unfortunately, I don't.
不幸的是，我不知道。

789
00:31:40.890 --> 00:31:44.570
But maybe I can find that out and reveal that in a future episode.
但也许我能查出来，并在以后的节目中揭晓。

790
00:31:44.570 --> 00:31:46.510
And then, so finally, two more gifts.
然后，最后还有两件礼物。

791
00:31:46.710 --> 00:31:51.610
Meredith got Dwight some shot glasses from Cancun, and Kevin got himself a foot bath.
梅雷迪思给德怀特买了一些来自坎昆的烈酒杯，凯文给自己买了一个泡脚盆。

792
00:31:51.810 --> 00:31:56.950
Guys, around 5 minutes, 55 seconds, there is a scene where Michael is talking to Jim at
大家，在大约5分55秒的时候，有一个场景是迈克尔在吉姆的

793
00:31:56.950 --> 00:31:57.430
Jim's desk.
办公桌旁和吉姆谈话。

794
00:31:57.470 --> 00:32:01.410
This is when he reveals that he got Ryan for Secret Santa.
这就是他透露自己在秘密圣诞老人活动中抽到了瑞安的时候。

795
00:32:01.970 --> 00:32:05.390
And I just want to say, you see a ton of background action.
我只想说，你能看到大量的背景动作。

796
00:32:05.850 --> 00:32:07.670
Angela, you're walking from reception.
安吉拉，你正从前台走过来。

797
00:32:08.130 --> 00:32:10.910
Over Steve's shoulder, you see Toby and Mindy talking.
在史蒂夫的肩膀上方，你能看到托比和明迪在聊天。

798
00:32:11.150 --> 00:32:11.370
Yeah.
是的。

799
00:32:11.890 --> 00:32:14.350
They are 100% not in character.
他们百分之百没有在演角色。

800
00:32:14.570 --> 00:32:16.210
Not in character at all.
一点都没有在演角色。

801
00:32:16.430 --> 00:32:17.150
I saw that, too.
我也看到了。

802
00:32:17.230 --> 00:32:21.410
I was like, they're just talking about probably something in the writer's room or a story pitch,
当时我想，他们可能只是在聊编剧室里的事或者某个故事创意，

803
00:32:21.470 --> 00:32:22.750
or they're just having a conversation.
或者他们只是在闲聊。

804
00:32:23.270 --> 00:32:23.470
Yeah.
对。

805
00:32:23.570 --> 00:32:25.390
I mean, Paul is just being Paul.
我的意思是，保罗就是本色出演。

806
00:32:25.570 --> 00:32:25.670
Yeah.
对。

807
00:32:25.830 --> 00:32:30.170
If anyone's curious, the difference between Toby and Paul, go to 5 minutes, 55 seconds,
如果有人好奇托比和保罗的区别，可以快进到5分55秒，

808
00:32:30.210 --> 00:32:32.710
and you can see Paul and Mindy having a conversation in the background.
你能看到保罗和敏迪在背景里聊天。

809
00:32:32.810 --> 00:32:33.450
Yeah, exactly.
对，没错。

810
00:32:35.210 --> 00:32:36.090
Tree lighting.
点亮圣诞树。

811
00:32:36.550 --> 00:32:36.950
Okay.
好吧。

812
00:32:37.050 --> 00:32:38.470
I've been waiting for this moment.
我一直在等这一刻。

813
00:32:38.950 --> 00:32:40.070
The Christmas tree lighting.
圣诞树亮灯。

814
00:32:40.750 --> 00:32:44.970
This starts the beginning of Everyone Happy Angela Pissed.
这就拉开了“人人开心，安吉拉气炸”的序幕。

815
00:32:46.510 --> 00:32:50.590
So, this Christmas tree, the top of it has been hacked off by Kevin.
所以这棵圣诞树，树顶被凯文锯掉了。

816
00:32:50.790 --> 00:32:54.330
It is covered in so much tinsel.
上面挂满了金属饰条。

817
00:32:54.510 --> 00:32:54.750
Yeah.
对。

818
00:32:55.150 --> 00:32:56.170
So much tinsel.
挂了好多金属饰条。

819
00:32:56.390 --> 00:32:58.930
It has a smattering of just blue and red ball ornaments.
上面稀稀拉拉地挂着几个蓝红相间的球形饰品。

820
00:32:58.930 --> 00:33:00.910
It's just not their best effort.
这实在谈不上是他们的巅峰之作。

821
00:33:01.170 --> 00:33:06.090
And then it has the tiniest of tiny white lights, thanks to Phyllis.
然后上面还点缀着极少极小的白炽灯，多亏了菲莉丝。

822
00:33:06.290 --> 00:33:07.890
So, Dwight makes a big deal of it.
所以，德怀特小题大做了起来。

823
00:33:08.050 --> 00:33:11.770
He, like, takes the, like, the outlet, like, the plug.
他一把抓过那个，那个插座，就像是那个插头。

824
00:33:11.890 --> 00:33:12.530
What do you call it?
那叫什么来着？

825
00:33:13.090 --> 00:33:13.750
The plug?
插头？

826
00:33:13.850 --> 00:33:14.390
The plug.
插头。

827
00:33:14.530 --> 00:33:16.050
He takes the plug from Stanley.
他从斯坦利手里抢过了插头。

828
00:33:16.050 --> 00:33:17.070
He wants to plug it in.
他想要把它插上。

829
00:33:17.110 --> 00:33:18.330
He's like, just like Rockefeller Center.
他说，就像洛克菲勒中心一样。

830
00:33:18.330 --> 00:33:24.270
And everyone gathers around, and it's like, and Phyllis is like, I'm sorry.
大家都围了过来，感觉就像是，然后菲莉丝说，不好意思。

831
00:33:24.530 --> 00:33:30.350
And at six minutes, 38 seconds, you see my first pissed off face.
在6分38秒时，你能看到我第一次气急败坏的表情。

832
00:33:30.810 --> 00:33:32.030
Dang it, Phyllis.
可恶啊，菲莉丝。

833
00:33:32.210 --> 00:33:35.810
It's also one of those moments where I feel like Angela is like, I knew it.
这也是那种让我觉得安吉拉在想“我早就知道了”的时刻之一。

834
00:33:35.930 --> 00:33:36.470
I knew it.
我早就知道了。

835
00:33:36.470 --> 00:33:38.910
I knew I couldn't trust her to do these lights.
我早就知道不能指望她来弄这些彩灯。

836
00:33:39.090 --> 00:33:41.190
Why do I even have her do anything?
我为什么还要让她干任何事？

837
00:33:41.230 --> 00:33:41.410
Ever.
永远。

838
00:33:41.810 --> 00:33:42.690
Why do you have anyone do anything?
你为什么会让任何人干任何事？

839
00:33:42.770 --> 00:33:43.010
Yeah.
对。

840
00:33:43.550 --> 00:33:45.530
You can't let anyone do anything.
你谁都不能让任何人做任何事。

841
00:33:45.710 --> 00:33:46.670
These people are worthless.
这些人全都没用。

842
00:33:46.930 --> 00:33:47.330
Exactly.
没错。

843
00:33:47.970 --> 00:33:52.670
You know, that Christmas tree light thing is based on a real thing from Mike Schur's life.
你知道吗，那个圣诞树亮灯的桥段取材于迈克·舒尔生活中的真实经历。

844
00:33:52.990 --> 00:33:53.650
I know.
我知道。

845
00:33:55.070 --> 00:33:59.570
He said that when he and his wife got their first tree in New York, he bought a bunch
他说他和妻子在纽约买第一棵树的时候，他买了很多小灯泡缠在树上，结果插上电之后，

846
00:33:59.570 --> 00:34:03.310
of small lights for the tree, and he wrapped them around, and when he plugged it in, you
几乎根本看不到灯光。

847
00:34:03.310 --> 00:34:04.190
couldn't really see them.
我太喜欢这个了。

848
00:34:05.970 --> 00:34:06.910
I love that.
我喜欢编剧把他们现实生活中的那些小片段融入到剧集里。

849
00:34:06.910 --> 00:34:10.710
I love when writers work those little moments from their real life into the show.
我想说的是，说到那些本色出演而不是在演角色的演员们，

850
00:34:11.030 --> 00:34:15.010
I thought, speaking about people who are acting like themselves instead of their characters,
我想说的是，说到那些本色出演而不是在演角色的演员们，

851
00:34:15.010 --> 00:34:18.810
I thought Jim's talking head about Creed's gift is so John.
我觉得吉姆关于克里德礼物的访谈太有他的风格了。

852
00:34:19.110 --> 00:34:19.850
It is John.
确实很有他的风格。

853
00:34:20.070 --> 00:34:21.530
That is John right there.
那简直就是吉姆本姆。

854
00:34:21.650 --> 00:34:21.830
Yeah.
对啊。

855
00:34:22.130 --> 00:34:25.550
All the delivery, the smile, all of it.
那种语气、微笑，全都有。

856
00:34:25.810 --> 00:34:28.510
And then, of course, Creed's talking head made me laugh so hard.
然后呢，当然，克里德的访谈片段把我笑得不行。

857
00:34:28.770 --> 00:34:30.830
Creed is very funny in this episode.
克里德这一集里超级搞笑。

858
00:34:31.010 --> 00:34:36.050
I mean, everybody has some great moments, but Creed cracked me up a bunch in this episode.
我是说，每个人都有很棒的时刻，但克里德这一集把我逗笑了好多次。

859
00:34:36.050 --> 00:34:37.990
So now, Secret Santa is starting.
那么现在，秘密圣诞老人环节开始了。

860
00:34:38.230 --> 00:34:38.410
Yep.
没错。

861
00:34:38.690 --> 00:34:41.430
And everyone is gathered around in some office chairs.
大家都坐在几把办公椅上围成一圈。

862
00:34:41.770 --> 00:34:46.430
And I want to say, truly, I know we were joking about Charles McDougal, but the amount
我想说，真的，我知道我们之前在拿查尔斯·麦克杜格尔开玩笑，但他为了展现

863
00:34:46.430 --> 00:34:53.630
of energy and movement that he uses the camera to give this scene of people sitting in a circle,
大家围坐一圈的场景，运用镜头所营造出的那种活力与动感，

864
00:34:53.630 --> 00:34:56.810
I mean, it is impressive from a directorial standpoint.
我是说，从导演的角度来看这令人印象深刻。

865
00:34:56.810 --> 00:35:03.970
I think, like, I don't want to be crazy, but I think, like, film students should study this
我觉得，呃，我不想显得太夸张，但我觉得，呃，电影专业的学生真该好好研究这一段，

866
00:35:03.970 --> 00:35:10.010
portion of the episode because I'm imagining myself trying to film a group of people sitting
因为我想象了一下自己去拍一群人围坐一圈交换礼物，

867
00:35:10.010 --> 00:35:13.310
in a circle doing a gift exchange, and it would not look nearly this dynamic.
绝对拍不出这种动感。

868
00:35:13.530 --> 00:35:15.090
It's really, really impressive directing.
这导演水平真的是太厉害了。

869
00:35:15.350 --> 00:35:16.290
No, he's great.
没错，他很棒。

870
00:35:16.410 --> 00:35:17.350
He is really great.
他是真的很棒。

871
00:35:17.550 --> 00:35:20.950
Okay, so we're starting the Secret Santa, and Pam opens Jim's teapot.
好的，秘密圣诞老人开始了，帕姆打开了吉姆送的茶壶。

872
00:35:21.490 --> 00:35:25.550
She loves it, but Dwight moves things along so quickly that she doesn't have time to
她很喜欢，但德怀特催得太快了，她根本没时间

873
00:35:25.550 --> 00:35:27.890
look inside or notice the card that's in the box.
往里面看，也没注意到盒子里还有张卡片。

874
00:35:27.890 --> 00:35:29.830
Yeah, Dwight wants no chitty chat between gifts.
对，德怀特不希望礼物和礼物之间有任何闲聊。

875
00:35:29.970 --> 00:35:30.750
He's like, go, go, go, go, go.
他就像是在说，快快快快快。

876
00:35:30.850 --> 00:35:32.150
He's me coming in today.
他就像今天刚来上班的我。

877
00:35:32.290 --> 00:35:32.730
He is.
确实是。

878
00:35:32.750 --> 00:35:34.210
He's like, save it for the mic.
他就像在说，留着到麦克风前再聊吧。

879
00:35:34.870 --> 00:35:36.330
So he's moving things along.
所以他在催着大家继续。

880
00:35:36.450 --> 00:35:37.010
So it's Pam.
接下来轮到帕姆了。

881
00:35:37.250 --> 00:35:38.310
And then the next one.
然后是下一个。

882
00:35:38.430 --> 00:35:45.030
We find out that Michael buys Ryan a video iPod that costs $400.
我们发现迈克尔给瑞安买了一个价值400美元的视频iPod。

883
00:35:45.710 --> 00:35:47.690
You guys, this was not product placement.
伙计们，这可不是产品植入。

884
00:35:47.930 --> 00:35:48.510
It was not.
真不是。

885
00:35:48.690 --> 00:35:50.310
So many people wanted to know.
有好多人都在问。

886
00:35:50.450 --> 00:35:52.170
Yeah, we were not paid.
对，我们没拿赞助费。

887
00:35:52.170 --> 00:35:55.350
It was just sort of a really cool topical gift at the time.
它只是当时那种非常酷、很应景的礼物。

888
00:35:55.350 --> 00:35:55.630
Yeah.
对。

889
00:35:55.990 --> 00:36:00.170
And they were trying to think of a gift that would sort of be a showstopper that Michael
他们当时在想一件能压全场、迈克尔会觉得超级震撼、

890
00:36:00.170 --> 00:36:02.850
would think was very impressive that everyone would want.
而且所有人都想要的礼物。

891
00:36:03.250 --> 00:36:04.430
So this was coincidence.
所以这只是个巧合。

892
00:36:04.430 --> 00:36:05.770
We weren't paid to use it.
我们没收钱去用它。

893
00:36:05.910 --> 00:36:06.910
So I read that.
我看到过这个说法。

894
00:36:07.950 --> 00:36:09.090
Well, here's something.
好了，还有个事。

895
00:36:09.370 --> 00:36:12.430
A ton of people wanted to know who kept it at the end.
超级多的人想知道最后是谁把这东西留下了。

896
00:36:12.530 --> 00:36:12.810
Nobody.
谁都没留。

897
00:36:13.070 --> 00:36:14.690
We weren't allowed to keep any of the stuff.
我们根本不被允许留下任何东西。

898
00:36:14.910 --> 00:36:19.890
It all goes into a giant warehouse, and it gets labeled for the episode for props
它们全都会被送到一个巨大的仓库里，然后贴上道具标签，

899
00:36:19.890 --> 00:36:23.750
because if for some reason we have to go back and reshoot something,
因为万一由于某种原因我们需要回去补拍镜头，

900
00:36:23.750 --> 00:36:25.850
they take it off the shelf and they bring it back in.
他们就会把东西从架子上拿下来，再重新拿回片场。

901
00:36:25.970 --> 00:36:26.490
That's true.
确实如此。

902
00:36:26.610 --> 00:36:29.530
I don't know what happens after it's been in the warehouse for a while,
我不知道它在仓库里呆了一段时间后会怎么样，

903
00:36:29.530 --> 00:36:31.350
but it just goes to prop house storage.
但它就是去了道具库。

904
00:36:31.770 --> 00:36:35.330
I feel like it's still in a box labeled the office Christmas party.
我觉得它大概还在一个写着“办公室圣诞派对”的箱子里。

905
00:36:35.470 --> 00:36:36.330
It probably is.
很可能还在。

906
00:36:36.610 --> 00:36:38.830
There was a fan question from Beard Up, Beard Down.
有一个来自“留须党”的粉丝提问，

907
00:36:39.030 --> 00:36:40.750
Was the iPod sponsored by Apple?
那个iPod是苹果公司赞助的吗？

908
00:36:40.890 --> 00:36:41.590
It wasn't.
并不是。

909
00:36:41.670 --> 00:36:42.750
We said it was not.
我们说过不是。

910
00:36:42.930 --> 00:36:44.150
It's just a total coincidence.
这完全是个巧合。

911
00:36:44.150 --> 00:36:46.010
But there's more coincidence.
但还有更巧的。

912
00:36:46.890 --> 00:36:50.590
So the week after this episode aired,
就在这一集播出的一周后，

913
00:36:50.870 --> 00:36:56.450
Apple revealed that you could now download episodes of The Office onto these video iPods.
苹果透露，你现在可以将《办公室》的剧集下载到这些视频iPod上了。

914
00:36:56.610 --> 00:36:58.550
Again, this was not planned.
再次说明，这不是计划好的。

915
00:36:58.750 --> 00:37:04.470
And then The Office became the number one downloaded show on iTunes.
然后《办公室》就成了iTunes上下载量排名第一的节目。

916
00:37:04.790 --> 00:37:05.330
Yes.
是的。

917
00:37:05.690 --> 00:37:07.230
The number one downloaded show.
下载量排名第一的节目。

918
00:37:07.230 --> 00:37:09.670
I remember Rainn Wilson turned to me and said,
我记得雷恩·威尔森转向我对我说，

919
00:37:09.830 --> 00:37:11.570
I think we're going to make it.
我想我们要成功了。

920
00:37:11.970 --> 00:37:13.090
I think we're going to.
我想我们会的。

921
00:37:13.230 --> 00:37:16.350
This was the first moment it felt like the tide was turning for us
这是我们第一次感觉到风向开始转变，

922
00:37:16.350 --> 00:37:17.710
and that we might not get canceled.
我们可能不会被砍了。

923
00:37:18.010 --> 00:37:18.390
All right.
好吧。

924
00:37:18.550 --> 00:37:20.790
So next up, Michael gets his gift,
接下来，迈克尔收到了他的礼物，

925
00:37:21.210 --> 00:37:24.530
the oven mitt knitted by Phyllis.
菲利丝织的隔热手套。

926
00:37:24.810 --> 00:37:25.110
Oof.
哎哟。

927
00:37:25.590 --> 00:37:27.930
Now everyone had a $20 limit, you guys.
各位，当时每个人的预算限额是20美元。

928
00:37:28.130 --> 00:37:30.490
That's why this iPod really shakes everything up
这就是为什么这个iPod彻底打破了平衡，

929
00:37:30.490 --> 00:37:32.070
because he spent $400.
因为他花了400美元。

930
00:37:32.470 --> 00:37:32.810
Yes.
没错。

931
00:37:33.070 --> 00:37:33.510
Yes.
对。

932
00:37:34.090 --> 00:37:36.210
And he has his line where he says,
他有句台词，他说，

