00:43:32.760 --> 00:43:34.180
blogs slash journals.
博客兼日记里了。

1092
00:43:34.440 --> 00:43:35.640
I'm living for this.
我太期待这个了。

1093
00:43:35.720 --> 00:43:37.060
I can't wait to hear about it.
我迫不及待想听了。

1094
00:43:37.200 --> 00:43:37.460
All right.
好吧。

1095
00:43:37.600 --> 00:43:38.160
I do have to pee.
我确实得去个洗手间。

1096
00:43:38.980 --> 00:43:42.700
Oh, do you want me to give you some snow facts when we come back from the break?
噢，你想让我等我们休息回来后再讲雪的冷知识吗？

1097
00:43:42.980 --> 00:43:43.680
I mean, can I go pee?
我是说，我能去上个厕所吗？

1098
00:43:43.680 --> 00:43:47.080
You should be on an empty bladder when I lay these awesome facts on you.
等我给你们抛出这些超赞的冷知识时，你们最好先把膀胱清空。

1099
00:43:47.260 --> 00:43:50.000
You don't tell me or my bladder what we're doing.
你可别替我和我的膀胱做决定我们要干嘛。

1100
00:43:50.000 --> 00:43:50.900
Well, what do you want?
好吧，你到底想怎样？

1101
00:43:51.000 --> 00:43:54.480
Do you want full bladder snow facts or empty bladder snow facts?
你想听憋尿时的雪地冷知识，还是放空后的雪地冷知识？

1102
00:43:54.520 --> 00:43:55.880
I want empty bladder snow facts.
我想听放空后的雪地冷知识。

1103
00:43:55.900 --> 00:43:56.200
All right.
好吧。

1104
00:43:56.200 --> 00:43:57.180
That's what I'm saying.
我就是这个意思。

1105
00:43:57.420 --> 00:44:01.180
Oh, I thought you were telling me that I had to not drink any more water or tea.
哦，我还以为你是让我别再喝水或喝茶了。

1106
00:44:01.680 --> 00:44:05.160
When we go on a road trip, my husband will be like, can you not get an iced tea?
每次我们去自驾游，我老公就会说，你能不能别买冰茶了？

1107
00:44:05.980 --> 00:44:12.320
Okay, clearly you're projecting some other thing on me because I said I thought you should
好吧，很明显你在把别的事投射到我身上，因为我说我以为你应该

1108
00:44:12.320 --> 00:44:14.660
empty your bladder for the snow facts she's leaving.
为了她要留下的雪地冷知识去上个厕所。

1109
00:44:14.880 --> 00:44:17.520
First, you push away from the mic to eat your snack.
首先，你把身子往后移开麦克风去吃零食了。

1110
00:44:17.940 --> 00:44:18.940
This is for you, Jenna.
这是给你的，珍娜。

1111
00:44:21.550 --> 00:44:22.390
It's so disgusting.
太恶心了。

1112
00:44:22.490 --> 00:44:23.790
Love the high nut Cheerios.
真喜欢高坚果味的幸运麦圈。

1113
00:44:24.550 --> 00:44:25.390
Oh, God.
噢，天哪。

1114
00:44:31.680 --> 00:44:36.000
For letting me have my bathroom break, I want to hear all about your snow.
为了让我去上洗手间，我想听听你关于雪的一切。

1115
00:44:36.000 --> 00:44:36.640
All right.
好吧。

1116
00:44:36.640 --> 00:44:42.260
I hope this isn't anticlimactic for people, but the company that came to make the snow
我希望这对大家来说不会虎头蛇尾，不过来造雪的那家公司

1117
00:44:42.260 --> 00:44:43.580
is called Snow Business.
叫做“造雪业务”。

1118
00:44:44.020 --> 00:44:45.540
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

1119
00:44:45.840 --> 00:44:46.520
Snow Business.
造雪业务。

1120
00:44:46.740 --> 00:44:47.540
Snow Business.
造雪业务。

1121
00:44:47.540 --> 00:44:48.340
I remembered.
我记住了。

1122
00:44:48.620 --> 00:44:49.800
I remembered that.
我把这个记住了。

1123
00:44:50.040 --> 00:44:51.060
It so tickled me.
这把我逗乐得不行。

1124
00:44:51.440 --> 00:44:53.960
Okay, so here's how it works with fake snow.
好啦，人工雪是这样的。

1125
00:44:54.280 --> 00:44:56.220
There's a guy from Snow Business.
有个来自造雪业务公司的人。

1126
00:44:56.220 --> 00:44:57.360
He shows up.
他出现了。

1127
00:44:57.740 --> 00:45:03.420
Now, the snow that falls from the sky is different from the ground cover snow.
现在，从天上落下来的雪和地上的雪是不一样的。

1128
00:45:03.420 --> 00:45:05.680
The snow on the ground is snow.
地上的雪就是雪。

1129
00:45:05.940 --> 00:45:11.340
The snow that falls from the sky, I know, because it falls on my character at the end,
从天上落下来的雪，我知道，因为它最后落在了我的角色身上，

1130
00:45:11.360 --> 00:45:13.060
and it is not snow.
而且那不是雪。

1131
00:45:13.180 --> 00:45:14.100
It's not snow.
那不是雪。

1132
00:45:14.100 --> 00:45:14.980
It's soap.
那是肥皂。

1133
00:45:15.240 --> 00:45:15.760
Yes.
没错。

1134
00:45:15.760 --> 00:45:17.140
You can get a choice.
你可以有选择。

1135
00:45:17.360 --> 00:45:21.360
You can get a choice of cornstarch, plastic, or soap.
你可以选择玉米淀粉、塑料或肥皂。

1136
00:45:21.940 --> 00:45:25.600
And Greg watched a demonstration of all three, and he picked soap.
格雷格观看了这三种材料的演示，然后他选了肥皂。

1137
00:45:25.840 --> 00:45:32.480
Well, when by accident, a little piece of that might get in your mouth, it tastes like soap.
好吧，当不小心有一小块那东西进到你嘴里时，尝起来就像肥皂。

1138
00:45:32.480 --> 00:45:35.500
Because I shriek, and a piece of it went in my mouth.
因为我尖叫了一声，然后有一小块进我嘴里了。

1139
00:45:36.600 --> 00:45:38.340
That's what she said.
她就是这么说的。

1140
00:45:38.740 --> 00:45:39.000
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

1141
00:45:39.420 --> 00:45:39.760
Okay.
好吧。

1142
00:45:40.080 --> 00:45:42.140
On the ground, though, it's real snow.
不过在地上，那是真雪。

1143
00:45:42.460 --> 00:45:45.940
And they bring this machine, and I don't know exactly how it works,
他们带来了这台机器，我不知道它具体是怎么运作的，

1144
00:45:46.040 --> 00:45:50.060
but it's kind of like a wood chipper, but in reverse.
但它有点像碎木机，不过是反过来的。

1145
00:45:50.500 --> 00:45:52.840
It looks like something out of a Dr. Seuss book.
它看起来像是苏斯博士书里蹦出来的东西。

1146
00:45:52.900 --> 00:45:53.600
It does.
确实是。

1147
00:45:53.900 --> 00:45:54.800
It really does.
真的特别像。

1148
00:45:55.020 --> 00:45:57.380
And it really blows snow.
而且它真的能吹出雪。

1149
00:45:57.640 --> 00:45:58.980
I guess that's what it looks like.
我想它看起来就是那样吧。

1150
00:45:58.980 --> 00:46:01.520
It looks like a snowblower, but it generates snow.
它看起来像个吹雪机，但它能制造出雪。

1151
00:46:01.760 --> 00:46:06.140
And then it just blows it all over the ground, all over the cars, and all that stuff.
然后这东西就把雪吹得到处都是，满地都是，车上也是，各种地方都是。

1152
00:46:06.360 --> 00:46:11.920
But guys, remember, this is like, we're shooting this in October in Los Angeles,
但是各位，记住，我们当时是在十月份的洛杉矶拍摄的，

1153
00:46:11.920 --> 00:46:13.960
and it's hot in October.
十月份天气很热。

1154
00:46:14.000 --> 00:46:15.720
It stays warm here.
这里一直很暖和。

1155
00:46:15.940 --> 00:46:19.200
In the daytime, it's still in the mid-80s, 90s.
白天温度还在八十几度、九十度左右。

1156
00:46:19.760 --> 00:46:23.600
But it was night, and so we had a little bit of time with it.
不过那是晚上，所以我们有一点时间来处理它。

1157
00:46:23.600 --> 00:46:26.040
I mean, it was still warm out, but...
我是说，外面其实还是挺暖和的，但是……

1158
00:46:26.040 --> 00:46:28.280
Yeah, it was probably like in the high 60s.
对，大概有快七十度的样子吧。

1159
00:46:28.400 --> 00:46:30.100
Yeah, that sounds about right.
对，差不多是这样。

1160
00:46:30.400 --> 00:46:30.600
All right.
好吧。

1161
00:46:30.600 --> 00:46:35.000
But yes, we were very excited to have snow, and Jenna, we're...
不过对，我们很高兴能有雪，而且珍娜，我们……

1162
00:46:35.000 --> 00:46:36.220
Did you like my snow facts?
你们喜欢我的雪花冷知识吗？

1163
00:46:36.540 --> 00:46:40.180
I feel a little vulnerable about them now, because we set them up so much.
我现在觉得有点没底了，因为我们前面铺垫了那么多。

1164
00:46:40.280 --> 00:46:43.620
I mean, there was like a break, and in my head about it.
我是说，中间好像休息了一下，我脑子里一直在想这事。

1165
00:46:43.860 --> 00:46:45.020
I like your snow facts.
我喜欢你的雪花冷知识。

1166
00:46:45.260 --> 00:46:45.900
Snow business.
冰雪生意。

1167
00:46:46.280 --> 00:46:47.060
That's cute.
真可爱。

1168
00:46:47.320 --> 00:46:49.180
I think snow business is really cute.
我觉得冰雪生意真的很可爱。

1169
00:46:49.380 --> 00:46:49.760
All right.
好吧。

1170
00:46:49.760 --> 00:46:52.820
But let's go back to the gift exchange.
但我们还是回到交换礼物环节吧。

1171
00:46:53.220 --> 00:46:59.520
This is when Kelly gets Angela's poster, but Angela, you do get to take it back.
这段是凯莉拿到了安吉拉的海报，不过安吉拉，你后来确实把它拿回来了。

1172
00:46:59.860 --> 00:47:00.960
Okay, here's the thing.
好吧，情况是这样的。

1173
00:47:01.100 --> 00:47:08.140
I wrote in my MySpace blog about this moment, and I wrote that it was one of the hardest
我在我的MySpace博客上写过这一幕，我写道，这是我们演员阵容里最难熬过的

1174
00:47:08.140 --> 00:47:15.480
things for us to get through as a cast, that the first time Mindy unrolls the poster and
时刻之一。当敏迪第一次展开海报并

1175
00:47:15.480 --> 00:47:20.800
looks at it, and we all see it, we all, every person lost it.
看着它时，我们所有人都看到了，每个人，真的是每个人都笑崩了。

1176
00:47:20.880 --> 00:47:22.500
Because it's so ridiculous.
因为这太荒谬了。

1177
00:47:22.500 --> 00:47:23.320
It's so ridiculous.
简直太荒谬了。

1178
00:47:23.320 --> 00:47:24.760
We had not seen it.
我们之前都没见过。

1179
00:47:25.000 --> 00:47:31.060
It was an actual surprise to us while we were filming, and we all lost it.
拍摄时这对我们来说是个真正的惊喜，我们全都笑场了。

1180
00:47:31.200 --> 00:47:37.900
I had that, in fact, it was particularly hard on Rain for some reason, and that in one take,
我记得，事实上，不知为什么，这对雷恩来说尤其艰难，在其中一个镜头里，

1181
00:47:38.080 --> 00:47:41.300
he broke three times because he could not get through it.
他笑场了三次，根本没办法演下去。

1182
00:47:41.300 --> 00:47:47.160
I can't believe that Mindy was tasked with having to unroll that poster.
我简直不敢相信敏迪居然承担了展开那张海报的任务。

1183
00:47:47.580 --> 00:47:50.220
How did we ever get a shot of her not laughing?
我们到底是怎么拍到她不笑的镜头的？

1184
00:47:50.480 --> 00:47:53.020
I don't know, but we were cracking up.
我不知道，但我们当时真的笑疯了。

1185
00:47:53.240 --> 00:47:56.780
There's a little detail in that scene that made me laugh when I rewatched it, which is
那个场景里有个小细节，我重看的时候把我逗笑了，就是

1186
00:47:56.780 --> 00:48:02.100
how you just very subtly swat the oven mitt away on your way to getting the poster.
你在去拿海报的路上，非常顺手地把隔热手套给拍开的那一下。

1187
00:48:02.340 --> 00:48:03.120
That was all me.
那完全是我即兴发挥的。

1188
00:48:03.300 --> 00:48:04.200
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

1189
00:48:04.200 --> 00:48:05.800
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

1190
00:48:05.800 --> 00:48:07.440
It was such a good detail.
这个细节太棒了。

1191
00:48:07.700 --> 00:48:08.420
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

1192
00:48:09.420 --> 00:48:16.120
Um, well, in tracking the oven mitt, Meredith eventually takes the oven mitt.
嗯，顺着隔热手套这条线说，梅雷迪思最后拿走了那个隔热手套。

1193
00:48:17.020 --> 00:48:22.860
But, you know, Michael has to then call her a sucker and say that he wanted her to take
但是呢，迈克尔随后得管她叫冤大头，说他其实就是想让

1194
00:48:22.860 --> 00:48:26.000
it, and it was reverse psychology when he said he wanted to keep it.
她拿走，当他说想留着它时用的其实是反向心理学。

1195
00:48:26.160 --> 00:48:30.560
I love that he decided that he needed to break down reverse psychology to all of us, because
我太喜欢他决定向我们所有人都解释一下什么是反向心理学了，因为

1196
00:48:30.560 --> 00:48:31.660
I don't know if you've heard of it.
我不知道你们有没有听说过这词。

1197
00:48:31.800 --> 00:48:33.100
It's a pretty cool thing.
这可是个挺酷的东西。

1198
00:48:33.400 --> 00:48:35.360
I'm like, Michael, you're such an idiot.
当时我的反应是，迈克尔，你真是个大笨蛋。

1199
00:48:35.360 --> 00:48:40.440
Do you remember how Phyllis cried during that scene?
你还记得菲利丝在那个场景里是怎么哭的吗？

1200
00:48:40.720 --> 00:48:43.700
Yeah, she stayed in, like, sort of that sad place.
对，她一直沉浸在那种有点难过的状态里。

1201
00:48:43.940 --> 00:48:49.220
She cried for, like, a half hour, and in between takes of that, where she had to be crying,
她哭了差不多半个小时，而在拍摄那些需要她哭的镜头间隙，

1202
00:48:49.380 --> 00:48:50.740
